# ===================== NEW CLASSES =====================
class <app> [launch] : The only entry module. main() picks a view, builds the one Controller, hands both to the view. Replaces app + app_bootstrap + lifecycle + devices.
class Setup(Panel) [launch] : The setup panel. Scans ports and gamepads, validates an assignment, constructs Models into the Controller. Rendered by every view's PanelView from its schema, so there is one wizard instead of three.
class Controller [control] : Owns every Model. The ONLY object a view talks to. Constructs/destructs models on demand, serialises commands per model, wires the per-model estops into the global one, closes everything exactly once on exit.
class EventLog [control] : One event log (was Event + EventBus + ErrorRouter + three per-view popup managers). Module singleton `events`. One policy decides what needs an acknowledged popup.
class Event [control] : Plain record of one event. No behaviour beyond a merge key and serialisers.
class Result [control] : One result type (was CommandResult, Ok, Failed and as_result). Built only by Panel.run.
class Refused(Exception) [control] : Raised by a command to refuse. Cannot be silently dropped, which designs out finding 4 (refusals reported as Ok).
class NeedsConfirm(Exception) [control] : Raised by a command that must not proceed unattended; the view asks, then re-runs with confirmed=True.
class Panel [model] : Anything a view can render: a Param table, a schema, a state snapshot, and run(). Base of Model and Setup. Replaces the SchemaCommands mixin.
class Model(Panel) [model] : Base of every station model. Owns its Devices, opens/closes them on demand, reports their status in state, and carries the ONE estop latch implementation. Replaces the ManagedModel protocol and three hand-rolled latch copies.
class Param [model] : Typed, bounded parameter declaration. Unchanged.
class <schema> [model] : Schema element builders and the questions renderers ask. Gains `image` and per-state toggle args; otherwise unchanged.
class <plot_data> [model] : Red Percent CSV parsing and figure rendering, used by RedMonitor so all three views show the same image.
class ProbeMode [model] : DISABLED, IDLE (was ENABLED_IDLE), AUTO (was AUTONOMOUS), MANUAL, FAULT.
class Probe(Model) [model] : Mode machine, move/jog frames, position sampling, motion interlock. Owns a SerialPort and a Gamepad. Was BaseProbe (1682 lines); loses scripts, client liveness, gamepad plumbing and its private copy of the latch.
class StepperProbe(Probe) [model] : TMC2209 board.
class DCProbe(Probe) [model] : Own packet format; firmware cannot kill coils.
class ChuckPositioner(Probe) [model] : Stepper-family board.
class Heater(Model) [model] : Was TemperatureSystem. Owns a SerialPort.
class Rotator(Model) [model] : Was RotatorSystem. Owns an SMC100.
class RedMonitor(Model) [model] : Was RedPercentSystem. Owns a Screen. Follows a Probe for position.
class MonitorRun [model] : One monitoring run. Was MonitoringRun.
class RunLog [model] : Samples of one run. Was RedPercentDataLog.
class Device [device] : Base of everything a Model owns that touches the outside world: open(), close(), is_open, status. One way to report connection state upward.
class ConnectionState [device] : SIMULATED, CONNECTING, VERIFIED, UNVERIFIED, LOST, CLOSED.
class TransportError(Exception) [device] : Lives in the same module as SerialPort, which is the only thing that raises it.
class SerialPort(Device) [device] : Was `serial` (which shadowed pyserial). ONE write path with a priority lane and an in-lock abort check. Knows nothing about probes.
class SimulatedPort [device] : Stand-in pyserial object for simulator mode.
class SMC100(Device) [device] : Newport driver. Protocol methods keep their vendor names so upstream diffs stay readable; its raw port I/O moves onto SerialPort so the station has one transport stack.
class Gamepad(Device) [device] : Was ControllerPoller + BaseGamepad + four subclasses. Layouts become a data table. 'Controller' now means only the Controller.
class GamepadHub [device] : Was InputService. Process-wide owner of SDL and joystick claims.
class Screen(Device) [device] : Screen capture (mss). Was duplicated in RedPercentSystem and the web server.
class <theme> [view] : One shared look for all three views: role palette, toggle on/off roles, one base font size. Tk and Qt read it directly; the Web view serves it as CSS variables. Replaces per-widget hardcoded Arial 10, a 10px Qt stylesheet and a separate Web palette.
class Dashboard [view] : Toolkit-neutral dashboard logic shared by Tk and Qt: event popup policy, model open/close, global estop toggle, focus forwarding.
class PanelView [view] : Toolkit-neutral panel logic: gather inputs, run, confirm, show Refused, gate by mode, refresh. One abstract _make_<type> per schema element type, so a view missing a renderer cannot be instantiated.
class TkDashboard(Dashboard) [view-tk] : Tk window.
class TkPanelView(PanelView) [view-tk] : Tk renderer. Was DynamicView.
class ClosableNotebook [view-tk] : Pure widget. Was DraggableClosableNotebook.
class QtDashboard(Dashboard) [view-qt] : Qt window.
class QtPanelView(PanelView) [view-qt] : Qt renderer. Was QtDynamicView.
class SeriesPlot [view-qt] : Pure widget.
class RegionOverlay [view-qt] : Pure widget. Was SelectionOverlay. Qt event-handler names are fixed by Qt and exempt from the naming scheme.
class DeviceDock [view-qt] : Pure widget.
class WebView [view-web] : Was WebDashboardWindow + WebDashboardServer. Owns the HTTP server AND the browser-heartbeat watchdog, which calls Controller.estop_all. Client liveness no longer exists in any model.
class ApiHandler [view-web] : Thin JSON wrapper over the same Controller calls the desktop views make. Was WebAPIHandler + WebModelAdapter.

rel Setup ..> Controller : add(model)
rel <app> ..> Setup : builds
rel <app> ..> Controller : builds
rel Controller o-- Model : owns 0..*
rel Controller ..> EventLog : publishes
rel EventLog o-- Event
rel Panel ..> Result : run() returns
rel Panel ..> Param
rel Panel ..> <schema>
rel Model *-- Device : owns 1..*
rel Probe *-- SerialPort
rel Probe *-- Gamepad
rel Probe *-- ProbeMode
rel Heater *-- SerialPort
rel Rotator *-- SMC100
rel SMC100 *-- SerialPort
rel RedMonitor *-- Screen
rel RedMonitor *-- MonitorRun
rel MonitorRun *-- RunLog
rel RedMonitor ..> Probe : reads position
rel RedMonitor ..> <plot_data>
rel SerialPort *-- ConnectionState
rel SerialPort o-- SimulatedPort
rel SerialPort ..> TransportError : raises
rel Gamepad ..> GamepadHub : claim/release
rel Dashboard ..> Controller : only dependency
rel PanelView ..> Controller : schema/state/run
rel Dashboard o-- PanelView : one per open model
rel TkDashboard ..> Controller : holds (inherited)
rel QtDashboard ..> Controller : holds (inherited)
rel PanelView ..> <theme>
rel Dashboard ..> <theme>
rel WebView ..> <theme> : serves as CSS variables
rel TkDashboard o-- ClosableNotebook
rel QtDashboard o-- DeviceDock
rel QtPanelView o-- SeriesPlot
rel QtPanelView o-- RegionOverlay
rel WebView *-- ApiHandler
rel WebView ..> Controller : estop_all on lost heartbeat
rel ApiHandler ..> Controller : schema/state/run

# ===================== NEW MEMBERS (no old origin) =====================
+ Controller.reopen | method | reopen(name): add() again from the config remembered at remove(), so a reopened model is never headless.
+ Controller.schema | method | schema(name) -> dict. What a view renders.
+ Controller.is_active | prop | True while any model is moving or heating. What the Web heartbeat watchdog consults.
+ Controller.clear_estop_all | method | clear_estop_all(confirmed). One confirmation listing the latched models, then each model's own clear_estop.
+ Controller.is_estopped | prop | any(model.is_estopped). Drives the global toggle's label.
+ Controller.set_input_focus | method | Forwards window focus to every Gamepad gate. Views no longer reach into probes.
+ Model.devices | prop | The Devices this model owns.
+ Model.open | method | Open every owned Device. On demand.
+ Model.is_active | prop | Is it moving / heating / recording right now. Replaces three private _client_liveness_active copies.
+ Model.halt | method | Unlatched stop of motion/heat. Subclasses implement _halt_hardware only.
+ Model._halt_hardware | method | The ONE hook a subclass writes for stopping: the strongest hardware stop it has, sent on the priority lane.
+ Model.toggle_estop | method | Per-model stop/clear toggle command. Inherited, so every model has it and the Controller's global stop is just these wired together.
+ Model.state | prop | One snapshot dict: params, mode, is_estopped, fault, and each owned Device's status. How a model tells the Controller what it is.
+ Device.open | method | 
+ Device.close | method | 
+ Device.is_open | prop | 
+ Device.status | prop | ConnectionState or equivalent; surfaces in Model.state.
+ Screen.grab | method | grab(region) -> image.
+ RedMonitor.load_run | method | Load a saved CSV run for the analysis plot. Moved from the PySide-only PlotDialog into the model so all three views get it.
+ RedMonitor.set_plot_dims | method | Choose the analysis plot's dimensions.
+ RedMonitor.figure | prop | PNG bytes of the analysis plot, rendered once by plot_data.render_figure and displayed by every view.
+ <schema>.image | method | New element: an image the model supplies. Used by RedMonitor.figure.
+ <schema>.indicator | method | New element: read-only boolean lamp. Used for is_estopped / is_faulted.
+ PanelView._show_refused | method | Non-modal status line. Desktop views drop Refused today.
+ PanelView._make_element | method | Dispatches to one abstract _make_<type> per ELEMENT_TYPE.
+ Dashboard.open | method | 
+ Dashboard.toggle_estop_all | method | The global FULL STOP / CLEAR toggle: Controller.estop_all or clear_estop_all, label driven by Controller.is_estopped.
+ <theme>.ROLES | prop | neutral, go, danger, warning, info -> colours. One table.
+ <theme>.FONT_SIZE | prop | One base size; every widget derives from it. Overridable at launch (--font-size).
+ <theme>.toggle_colors | method | toggle_colors(on_role, off_role, is_on). A toggle declares what its ON state means, so a latched estop shows danger, not the green Tk paints every ON toggle today.
+ PanelView._apply_theme | method | 
+ Result.needs_confirm | prop | 

# ===================== FATE OF EVERY EXISTING METHOD =====================
@ <app> => <app>
main -> =
select_view -> .pick_view | verb scheme; 'select' is reserved for operator selections
run_legacy_app, run_pyside_app, run_web_app -> .launch | three 390-line launcher functions, each nesting its own setup wizard, become one launch(view_name) over a 3-entry table; the wizards are replaced by the Setup panel
launch_legacy, launch_pyside -> ! purged | one-line wrappers around run_*; pick_view returns the name

@ <app_bootstrap> => Setup
discover_ports -> .scan_ports
discover_controllers -> .scan_gamepads | 'controller' now means only the Controller
probe_device_at -> .identify
normalize_config -> ! implied | one Setup produces configs in one shape; there is nothing left to normalise
validate_assignment -> .validate
build_models, _build_each -> .build
link_models -> ! implied | Controller.add announces each model to the others (on_model_added); no second wiring pass

@ <model.devices> => Setup
_stepper, _dc, _chuck, _temperature, _rotator, _red_percent -> ! implied | every Model subclass has the same constructor signature and class attrs NAME / IDENTITY / NEEDS_PORT / NEEDS_GAMEPAD; MODEL_TYPES is a dict of classes
names -> .model_types
get, build -> .build

@ Device => Setup
__init__, build, __repr__ -> ! implied | the catalog record class (also named Device) is replaced by class attributes on each Model subclass

@ <lifecycle> => Controller
set_current_manager, current_manager -> ! implied | one Controller per process, created in launch() and never replaced; re-setup calls Controller.reset
shutdown -> .close
install_exit_hooks -> ._hook_exit
_reset_for_tests -> ! purged | no module globals remain to reset

@ SystemManager => Controller
__init__ -> =
subscribe -> =
unsubscribe -> =
_emit -> ._notify
register -> .add
release, _stop_then_teardown -> .remove | destruct on demand: estop, close devices, drop
get_model -> ._model | private: views never receive a model
get_config -> .config
get_active_models_snapshot -> .model_names
hide, show, is_hidden, visible_models -> ! purged | owner ruling 2026-09-21: closing a tab destructs the model (Controller.remove); reopening constructs it (Controller.add). No hidden state exists
shutdown_all -> .close
reconfigure -> .reset
full_stop_all -> .estop_all | wires the per-model estops together (owner ruling)
_stop_concurrently -> ._estop_concurrently
_report -> ! implied | EventLog is called directly

@ WebModelAdapter => Controller
__init__, set_system_manager -> ! implied | no adapter: the Web view holds the Controller like the other two views
_get_device_lock -> ._lock_for | per-model command serialisation now protects all three views, not only Web
scan_hardware, start_hardware_scan, get_scan_status -> Setup.scan | progress is part of Setup.state
initialize_setup, _initialize_setup_locked, initialize_system -> Setup.build
get_system_info, get_state -> .state | state() for everything, state(name) for one model
get_devices -> .model_names
_determine_connection_status, _transport_state -> Model.state | each owned Device reports status; no view-side inference
_schema_commands, _schema_options_commands, _schema_attrs -> Panel._allows | the schema allow-list moves into Panel.run, so it guards every view
resolve_options -> .options
dispatch_command -> .run
full_stop_all -> .estop_all
set_device_attribute -> .set_value
append_log, get_logs -> EventLog.info | the Web-only stdout buffer becomes ordinary info events
errors_since -> EventLog.since
latest_error_id -> EventLog.latest_id
record_client_heartbeat -> WebView.beat
client_heartbeat_age_seconds -> WebView.heartbeat_age

@ ClientLivenessGate => WebView
_init_client_liveness -> ! implied | WebView.__init__
_client_liveness_active -> Controller.is_active
touch_client_liveness -> .beat
stop_client_liveness_watchdog, _ensure_client_liveness_watchdog -> ! implied | the watchdog thread starts in WebView.open and ends in WebView.close
_client_liveness_loop -> ._watch_loop
_check_client_liveness -> ._check_heartbeat | on timeout: Controller.estop_all. One watchdog for the station instead of one per model

